WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.102
Were you very close to your father?

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.736
Yes.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.338
It was a daddy daughter kind of thing.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.239
Yeah, very much.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.641
What was he like as a father?

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.011
Very you know, adoring.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.645
Very sweet.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.413
Lisa Marie

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.215
Presley was just nine years old

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.549
when her father, Elvis died

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.718
from a heart attack in 1977.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.353
In 2003.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.821
She told Rolling Stone

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.456
that when her father kissed her goodnight

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.724
for the last time,

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:25.625
she had a feeling

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.327
something would happen, adding

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.862
she was obsessed with death

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.630
at a very early age.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.297
How did you deal with

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.333
all the attention of his death?

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.635
There was so many masses of people

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.637
mourning. That's what I meant.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.238
Yeah.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.874
In front of me fainting and carrying on.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.408
And I.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.709
I remember watching,

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.877
you know, as the casket was there.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.178
They were coming through and they were.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.546
There was a line.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.947
And I just remember

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:48.715
sitting on the stairwell

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.583
not knowing what to do with that.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.052
Lisa Marie was Elvis

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:52.552
and Priscilla

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.622
Presley's only child born in 1968

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.357
after her parents separated

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.758
when she was just four

00:00:58.758 --> 00:00:59.492
Lisa Marie

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.794
split her time between her

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.495
mom's house in Los Angeles

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.564
and her father's Graceland estate

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.865
in Memphis.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.001
Her childhood was far from perfect.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.603
After she began experimenting with drugs,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:13.073
her mother sent her to private school.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.008
In 2003, she told the L.A.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:15.842
Times.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.544
I never really fit into school.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.212
I didn't really have any direction.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.147
So

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.784
music was her escape.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:25.919
She went on to record

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.387
three studio albums.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.888
Her 2003 debut

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.757
album, to whom it may concern

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.458
reached number

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.359
five on the Billboard 200

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.261
and was certified gold.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.463
She performed duets

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:39.599
with the likes of Pat Benatar,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:41.968
not saying

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.370
I don't think that's allowed me.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.805
She once told Larry King

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.773
perhaps she was a bit

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.942
naive in choosing the same career

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:49.809
as her father.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.544
I've been a huge music lover.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.912
It's always had a huge impact on me.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.214
I want to write. I want to sing.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.816
I want to do the same thing for others.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.717
Have my music,

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.385
hopefully do that for others one day.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.520
Not realizing,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.989
you know what I sort of had to climb.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.090
I had an idea a little bit,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.958
but I think that I.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.493
I underestimated the whole thing.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.729
She recorded duets with her father

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.865
adding her voice to some of Elvis's

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.400
earlier recordings.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.238
Oh, please

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:21.875
help me get over it.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.744
Lisa Marie told ABC

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.779
she inherited a rebellious side

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.747
from her father.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.782
Alive and well in me.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.085
Yes.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:32.485
To the point

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.620
where my own children are like,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.522
Mom, stop.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.490
So what are you doing?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.158
Don't say that.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:38.725
You can't say that.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.426
I can't do that for decades.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.829
The tabloids tracked Lisa Marie Presley.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.197
The tabloids have been rough.

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.198
They're rough.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.065
They're really rough.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.434
Her love life always grabbed headlines.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:49.435
She was married

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.403
four times

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.704
She had two children with her

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.640
first husband, Danny Keough.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.942
Then just 20 days after they divorced,

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.611
she said, I do to Michael Jackson,

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.779
the king of Pop,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.314
when he wants to look into you

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.283
and he wants to intrigue you or capture

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.050
you or,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.384
you know,

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.885
whatever he wants to do with you.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.653
He can do it

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.490
The couple made

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.592
romantic music videos together

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.393
in stunned

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:16.329
audiences at the MTV Video Music Awards.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.698
Nobody thought this would last

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.639
but the marriage didn't last.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.708
They divorced in 1996

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.977
after about two years of marriage.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.846
She married actor Nicolas Cage in 2002.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.249
But they split after just three months.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.618
She tied the knot with Michael Lockwood

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:42.722
in 2006 and in 2008 gave birth to twins.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.858
By 2016 she had filed for divorce.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.961
Lisa Marie had a theory

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.262
about why her marriages

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.430
didn't work out

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.799
as she told the Daily Mail in 2003.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.068
It had to do with her own father.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.003
I'm looking for someone similar to him

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.072
and nobody could ever compare.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.974
He was so extraordinary, a presence,

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:01.808
she said.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.509
Not even as an entertainer,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.978
just as a person.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.246
With her father's death,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.380
Lisa Marie Presley

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.748
learned at an early age

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.383
what it means to grieve.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.084
Years later,

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:11.951
she would experience

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.620
tremendous grief again

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.288
when her 27 year old son,

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:18.124
Benjamin Keough, took his life in 2020.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:19.259
Last year,

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.593
Lisa Marie wrote an essay

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.395
about grief for People magazine.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.630
She wrote in part,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.931
Grief does not stop

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.899
or go away in any sense.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.702
A year or years after the loss, grief

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.203
is something

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.537
you will have to carry with you

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.139
for the rest of your life.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.174
Grief is incredibly lonely.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.143
It's a real choice to keep going.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.979
That's exactly what she did.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.180
Keep going.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.215
On Tuesday night,

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.516
she was on the red carpet

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.851
for the Golden Globes,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.886
where the movie Elvis about her father's

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.155
life was up for several awards

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.423
What did this movie mean

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.558
to you and your family? Everything.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.728
It just it's so incredible.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.630
There's no words.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.300
Lisa Marie Presley had a front row seat

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.367
to Austin Butler,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.669
winning the Golden Globe

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:05.204
for his portrayal of her father, Elvis.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.507
Some people wanted to put him in jail.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.142
Joel's movie

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.911
and have you gotten to know Austin Butler

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:12.578
a little bit?

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.447
Yeah, I'm going to grab now.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.215
Yes, a lot.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.784
A lot, actually.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:18.751
I adore him.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:19.919
She was asked that night

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.154
if she planned to keep in touch

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.322
with Austin Butler.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.390
Her answer was an emphatic yes.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:27.093
But fate intervened.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.662
Lisa Marie Presley was 54.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.930
Joining me now, CNN entertainment

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.666
reporter Chloe Melas. Chloe.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.235
What a heartbreaking week.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.638
What happened with Lisa Marie Presley?

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.307
We just saw her at the Golden Globes

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:44.210
right before this happened.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.378
Tell us about that and the

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.512
plans now to remember her.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.649
Jim, I was at the Golden Globes.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.317
I saw Lisa Marie.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.720
And like many of the reporters there,

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:54.921
we thought to ourselves

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.290
that she didn't seem like herself.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.358
We know

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.093
that a funeral details

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.127
are still forthcoming,

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:02.362
but she will be laid

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.197
to rest at Graceland,

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.165
where she was just earlier

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:06.933
this week,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.401
giving a speech like Kyung

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.602
said in her piece,

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.337
to remember her father,

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.373
what would have been his 80th birthday.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.073
And fans

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:14.907
were even

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:17.176
a little taken aback by her demeanor

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.378
and how she seemed.

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:20.780
Here's a little bit more of that speech

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:24.484
a few days ago that Lisa Marie gave

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:25.618
Thank you.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:26.619
I love you.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.354
It's been a while

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.157
I missed you.

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.698
And I love you.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.266
And you keep saying

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.100
you're the only people

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.535
that you're bringing me out of my house.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.773
I'm not kidding

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:48.274
you.

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.042
And I love you back.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.044
And that's why I'm here.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.381
So today

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:58.484
you would have been 80 years old.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.119
It's hard to believe

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.423
Jim, she's spoken

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.557
about the grief

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:05.425
that she suffered

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:08.361
after her son's suicide in 20. 20.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.095
She wrote about it

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.830
in an essay over the summer.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.665
And she said, My soul went with you.

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.767
And that she never fully recovered.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:15.635
It's only fitting

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.803
that she will be laid to rest

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:17.203
next to her

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.070
father and her

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.573
son, Benjamin, at Graceland.

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:21.741
And like we know,

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:22.442
we're all waiting

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:24.277
for a potential autopsy report,

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.711
but we might not get that.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.580
We might not ever get the details

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.782
as to what exactly happened.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:30.483
Jim

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:32.985
That's hard to hear.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.121
And it's just difficult to reflect

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:35.955
on how much pain

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.990
this family has gone through

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.625
over over the decades.

